ds 20.","id":"AC-2","seam":"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation","then":"The returned string starts with `- ` and still contains `(timestamp link unavailable)` and `0:10–0:20`. Red proof (pre-fix, unchanged tree): the returned string is exactly `Test Video (timestamp link unavailable) — 0:10–0:20` (title-independent symptom tail: `(timestamp link unavailable) — 0:10–0:20`) — it does not start with `- `, so the startsWith('- ') assertion fails red with that string in the failure output.","when":"formatCitation(citation) is called."},{"given":"A citation with source_type 'dynamous', lesson_url '' (empty), video_url '' (irrelevant on this path), non-empty snippet 'Test snippet text', start_seconds 10, end_seconds 20.","id":"AC-3","seam":"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation","then":"The returned string starts with `- `, contains no `](` (no markdown link), and still contains its blockquote line `> \"Test snippet text\"`. Red proof (pre-fix, unchanged tree): the return is `Test Video Title — 0:10–0:20\\n  > \"Test snippet text\"` — the snippet is kept but the `- ` marker is missing — so startsWith('- ') fails red on the unchanged tree.","when":"formatCitation(citation) is called."}],"dependencies":[],"invariants":["Every existing case in app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts keeps passing unchanged, including the exact console.warn message `[exportMarkdown] Skipping timestamp link — invalid video_url: \"<url>\"` emitted by both YouTube fallback paths.","The invalid-URL fallback still emits no markdown link (existing test pins not.toContain('[Test Video Title](')), and the Dynamous no-lesson_url fallback still emits no `](`.","Healthy paths are untouched: a valid YouTube URL keeps emitting `- [title](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=<id>&t=<start>s) — <range>\\n  > \"<snippet>\"` and a valid lesson_url keeps emitting `- [title](<lesson_url>) — <range>\\n  > \"<snippet>\"` (pinned by existing tests, including formatSources' `- [Test Video]`).","formatTimestamp, the blank/whitespace-snippet early return (''), formatSources' `**Sources:**` header and its newline join, the export header and the filename slug are unchanged; because formatSources joins entries with a single newline, each fallback entry must be a self-contained `- ` list item ending in its own blockquote line so consecutive entries no longer merge when rendered.","Only production file changed is app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts; test changes confined to app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts; no new or version-changed packages; no backend, schema, or protected-path files touched.","Unicode is load-bearing: em dash U+2014 between the title/marker segment and the range, en dash U+2013 inside the `0:10–0:20` range, and the two-space-indented `> \"<snippet>\"` blockquote line; tests must copy these characters exactly or the red/green signal is wrong."],"issue":{"number":49,"title":"fix(export): markdown export drops the transcript snippet when a citation URL cannot be parsed"},"out_of_scope":["Backend code, database schema, and any dependency additions or version changes (no new packages).","app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx, Message.tsx, ChatArea.tsx, Sidebar.tsx and any other component, hook or page.","The valid-URL and valid-lesson_url paths of formatCitation.","formatTimestamp, the export header and the filename slug in exportConversationAsMarkdown.","formatSources' joining logic and the `**Sources:**` header (only the strings formatCitation returns may change).","Any repository file other than app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts and app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts, and all protected/trust-root paths."],"risks":["Other modules importing formatCitation/formatSources were not exhaustively audited by the investigation; a consumer could depend on the current marker-less fallback shape. Mitigation: the change is confined to the three fallback return strings and every existing pinned assertion (console.warn text, not.toContain('[Test Video Title]('), not.toContain(']('), `- [Test Video]` in the formatSources tests) must stay green.","The fallback output mixes em dash (U+2014) and en dash (U+2013); an acceptance test that types ASCII hyphens will produce false red/green results. Copy the characters from the source templates and the expected_symptom verbatim.","The red loop is deferred: no existing command fails on the unchanged tree. The kernel's pre-change run must confirm the current suite is green (the investigation's green claim is a static trace) and that the new AC-1/AC-2 tests fail with `(timestamp link unavailable) — 0:10–0:20` visible in the failure output."],"summary":"In app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts, make every formatCitation fallback path emit the same shape as the healthy paths — a leading `- ` list marker plus the `> \"<snippet>\"` blockquote line. The two YouTube fallbacks (video_url unparseable, or parsed but with no `v` parameter) currently return `Test Video (timestamp link unavailable) — 0:10–0:20`, dropping the quoted transcript snippet entirely, and all three fallbacks (those two plus the Dynamous empty-lesson_url path, which keeps its snippet) omit the `- ` marker, so entries merge into the previous list item when the export is rendered. The fix adds the marker and the snippet line to the fallback returns only; healthy paths, formatTimestamp, formatSources, the header and the filename slug are untouched.","version":"2.0"},"sha256":"7e9b006e4d7ee85e4a438c7d1292e54708ee9bfaf6882420361b32b177daaa2c","source":"task-contract.json"},"design":{"content":{"ac_mapping":{"AC-1":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation"],"AC-2":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation"],"AC-3":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation"]},"allowed_new_files":[],"context_sha256":"c100f771f719f727f215d393fbb4f4215fb7670703814ff44dbee1468b69ade0","contract_sha256":"7e9b006e4d7ee85e4a438c7d1292e54708ee9bfaf6882420361b32b